                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "815fe3ca-64d8-345d-89cb-f784e19daca7",
                        "entry_id": "466cdac5-2db4-3d29-a84e-1ededd8a788f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a person: perverted or insane, originally supposedly due to the influence of the Moon; compare lunatic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "95a40ebd-fb69-466b-9886-63a6061c5478",
                                "sense_id": "815fe3ca-64d8-345d-89cb-f784e19daca7",
                                "text": "VVhat miſerie th' inabſtinence of Eve / Shall bring on men. […] all maladies / Of gaſtly Spaſm, or racking torture, qualmes / Of heart-ſick Agonie, all feavorous kinds, / Convulſions, Epilepſies, fierce Catarrhs, / Inteſtin Stone and Ulcer, Colic pangs, / Dæmoniac Phrenzie, moaping Melanchole / And Moon-ſtruck madneſs, pining Atrophie, / Maraſmus, and vvide-vvaſting Peſtilence, / Dropſies, and Aſthma's, and Joint-racking Rheums."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d606550-de4f-4f80-88a4-090745d0fdd5",
                                "sense_id": "815fe3ca-64d8-345d-89cb-f784e19daca7",
                                "text": "'Tvvas vvhen the Dog-ſtar's unpropitious ray / Smote ev'ry brain, and vvither'd ev'ry Bay; / Sick vvas the Sun, the Ovvl forſook his bovv'r, / The moon-ſtruck Prophet felt the madding hour: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3543227f-fd10-4234-81b6-b6c2e61d3496",
                                "sense_id": "815fe3ca-64d8-345d-89cb-f784e19daca7",
                                "text": "It may be that there have been many moonstruck and misleading ideals that have from time to time perplexed mankind. But assuredly there has been no ideal in practice so moonstruck and misleading as the ideal of practicality."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0947d9c3-4cb2-386a-a15c-bb680c410587",
                        "entry_id": "466cdac5-2db4-3d29-a84e-1ededd8a788f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Showing irrational behaviour, especially of a romantic or sentimental nature; in an entranced or distracted state, especially due to being in love."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ae7bc61-7b97-4cab-93d4-fb9f583b3f49",
                                "sense_id": "0947d9c3-4cb2-386a-a15c-bb680c410587",
                                "text": "[…] I, the moon-struck slave of Dora, perambulated round and round the house and garden for two hours, […] blowing kisses at the lights in the windows, and romantically calling on the night, at intervals, to shield my Dora—I don't know exactly what from, I suppose from fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7600be5b-1907-4c05-9917-fd27d309fbbd",
                                "sense_id": "0947d9c3-4cb2-386a-a15c-bb680c410587",
                                "text": "\"Up, Tristram, up,\" men cry, \"thou moonstruck knight! / What foul fiend rides thee? On into the fight!\" / —Above the din her voice is in my ears— / I see her form glide through the crossing spears,— / Iseult! … ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "05d22bb4-90eb-4352-a490-b99b8ed4de1f",
                                "sense_id": "0947d9c3-4cb2-386a-a15c-bb680c410587",
                                "text": "[W]e can also overlook the verbiage of a good deal of the mind-cure literature, some of which is so moonstruck with optimism and so vaguely expressed that an academically trained intellect finds it almost impossible to read it at all."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afbed03a-9038-4fbf-a3e7-5c01b254be41",
                                "sense_id": "0947d9c3-4cb2-386a-a15c-bb680c410587",
                                "text": "The full moon was spacious now behind the maples. The seedy Pickerbaugh domain was enchanted; […] and over all the world was the proper witchery of moonstruck love."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52c77cc9-134c-3c55-a806-e12e83897cd1",
                        "entry_id": "466cdac5-2db4-3d29-a84e-1ededd8a788f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Made physically sick, or (like fish) unsuitable for food, by the supposed effect of moonlight."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "regional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3d35188-10e4-4067-8c2c-41b9fd1e054f",
                                "sense_id": "52c77cc9-134c-3c55-a806-e12e83897cd1",
                                "text": "\"Yes, yes, thank God! I am not blind; I was afraid I was moon-struck.\" \"Moon-struck!\" uttered Carlos in astonishment. \"What do you mean?\" \"Why, don't you know,\" answered Antonio, \"that sleeping in the open air by moonlight often causes contractions, and sometimes makes persons blind whenever the moon shines?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed78e467-83d0-4647-b997-85319ccd0df2",
                        "source_entry_id": "466cdac5-2db4-3d29-a84e-1ededd8a788f",
                        "source_sense_description": "of a person: crazy or insane, originally supposedly due to the influence of the Moon — see also crazy, insane",
                        "target_lang_word": "lunatique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lunatique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8535a5ae-70a2-3cb3-ace2-b675c8c1000f",
                                        "entry_id": "63cc7283-754f-31d1-ae4a-4891d894f312",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est fantasque."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb57e385-b66f-4a5f-892f-40d531f14003",
                                                "sense_id": "8535a5ae-70a2-3cb3-ace2-b675c8c1000f",
                                                "text": "Entre ses numéros d’acteurs et ses sketches comiques, Érotissimo apparaît comme une aimable critique de la société française pompidolienne de 1968, à travers ses ouvriers rêveurs, ses employés feignants, ses concepteurs lunatiques et incompris, ses chefs d’entreprise âpres au gain et magouilleurs, ses fonctionnaires bornés et revanchards, tout cela confronté à l’évolution des mœurs de la nouvelle liberté sexuelle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01bfccf7-b9b2-461a-b2f3-846acb99e484",
                                                "sense_id": "8535a5ae-70a2-3cb3-ace2-b675c8c1000f",
                                                "text": "Le Jones dément, acculant au suicide sa secte d’arriérés, est à peine différent du lunatique Khadafi, le prophète de la lubie, du calamiteux Khomeini qui ayatollise gâteusement à Téhéran, ou du débile Lefebvre, qui rafistole à Écône sa petite église pour lui tout seul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f60eb764-9293-3916-9b24-18467e59a802",
                                        "entry_id": "63cc7283-754f-31d1-ae4a-4891d894f312",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est soumis à l’influence de la lune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39b1e928-3c37-30bf-9c4f-2ed192aa8ee5",
                                        "entry_id": "63cc7283-754f-31d1-ae4a-4891d894f312",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dont l’humeur est changeante ; cyclothymique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bed019a4-9bb1-302d-910c-d21714dfd1c8",
                                        "entry_id": "63cc7283-754f-31d1-ae4a-4891d894f312",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qualifiait un cheval qui est sujet à une ophtalmie périodique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Hippologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "150a0cab-e6a1-4e2c-b4c5-a1fcdbba28ff",
                                                "sense_id": "bed019a4-9bb1-302d-910c-d21714dfd1c8",
                                                "text": "[…] ; et une fois chez lui à deux ou trois cents kilomètres de distance, avant que le délai expire, un télégramme apprend au vendeur que son cheval est déclaré poussif, immobile, corneur ou lunatique, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ef6885f-e197-3914-8f6f-90716c40e85d",
                                        "entry_id": "63cc7283-754f-31d1-ae4a-4891d894f312",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est dans la lune, distrait."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Québec"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2856c23-5f57-4add-b9cb-4bed1c6b73c0",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef6885f-e197-3914-8f6f-90716c40e85d",
                                                "text": "Il aimait son côté lunatique, sa « tête de livres », qui se mariait à sa vivacité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lunatique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1da4615f-a5fd-323a-b71b-fa21da778ef9",
                                        "entry_id": "89707fef-bbb4-3d8a-aa76-2857958db32d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne lunatique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af924bd1-b1a1-4bd3-890b-3aa467148a60",
                                                "sense_id": "1da4615f-a5fd-323a-b71b-fa21da778ef9",
                                                "text": "D’ailleurs cette inégalité est le propre des lunatiques et dévoyés de cervelle ; elle existe aussi dans leurs gestes détraqués qui ne concordent pas exactement au sens des paroles, désaccord dont l’artiste habile peut tirer des effets comiques."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9e78b1f-95d1-4c1e-897c-9b0458507293",
                                                "sense_id": "1da4615f-a5fd-323a-b71b-fa21da778ef9",
                                                "text": "La lunatique, c’était elle, la baronne Blexen, et le juge Eggert, au contraire, était un homme contrôlé, vertueux et souverain de ses émotions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e19beb9c-4ffa-4311-9e41-e47d6ae1f6bc",
                                                "sense_id": "1da4615f-a5fd-323a-b71b-fa21da778ef9",
                                                "text": "Au milieu du siècle dernier, on traitait de songe-creux et de lunatiques ceux qui prétendaient aplanir les hiérarchies traditionnelles et renverser même la personne du Roi."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "98a24a58-a14c-4e36-ae08-54010df9582a",
